title: The Judgment Seat – Judgment, Hell and the Resurrection
description: Judgment, hell and the resurrection: now is the day of salvation, the judgment seat of Christ and our works tried by fire, the end of the wicked and the reality of eternal torment, the white throne, and the hope of the resurrection, from the teachings on judgment.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-judgment.html
highlight: judg; fire

# One deck for the doctrine "Judgment, hell & the resurrection" (68 teachings), its themes given equal weight.
# Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed. The verses the teachings typed out are shown from the KJV.

=== Introduction
--- The Judgment Seat [title]
overline: Doctrine · Judgment, hell & the resurrection
heading: The Judgment Seat
sub: The judgment seat, the end of the wicked, and today as the day of salvation.
refs: Hebrews 9:27; 2 Corinthians 5:10; 1 Corinthians 3:11-15; Revelation 20:11-15; 2 Corinthians 6:2
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 17543
--- Remember now thy Creator
big: Ecclesiastes 12:1 | mark: Remember now thy Creator in the days of thy youth
p: Solomon the king and preacher sums up the end of the matter. Remember thy Creator. Remember Him in your youth, while it is still light. Before the darkness of this life or the time to come, when it is too late.
p: There is a time it is too late to fear the Lord, to get right with Him, to remember our Creator.

=== Now is the day of salvation
# from 15287, 15288
--- Seek the LORD while he may be found
kicker: Now is the day of salvation
big: Isaiah 55:6 | mark: Seek ye the LORD while he may be found
p: Is there any judgment upon a nation as fearsome as their seeking the Lord and not being able to find Him, because He has withdrawn Himself from them? ([[Hosea 5:6]]) *Reprobate silver shall men call them* ([[Jeremiah 6:30]]).
p: The false idea that it is never too late with God, that as long as you live there's always a chance for salvation, has led so many to Hell. They put off to tomorrow the gift of grace. Like Pharaoh, they harden their hearts. Wake to Him and seek peace in Christ while you can.

# from 8549, 5878
--- To day if ye will hear his voice
kicker: Now is the day of salvation
big: Hebrews 4:7 | mark: To day if ye will hear his voice, harden not your hearts
p: Their unbelief in the desert prevented them from entering the promised land; so too fear your unbelief keeping you from entering into the rest in Jesus. *For we which have believed do enter into rest* ([[Hebrews 4:3]]). Note the tense.
p: God gives every opportunity to repent and believe on Jesus Christ, but it isn't limitless. Just as God was longsuffering as Noah built his ark, and then shut the door, too late to be saved, so too is His offer of grace ([[Genesis 7:16]]).
read: app:doctrine-judgment~15288 | Before it is too late, reprobate
read: app:doctrine-judgment~5878 | To day if ye will hear his voice

=== The judgment seat of Christ
# from 10477, 10803
--- Every man according to his works
kicker: The judgment seat
big: 2 Corinthians 5:10 | mark: For we must all appear before the judgment seat of Christ
p: You heard me. The Lord Jesus Christ will judge every man according to his works. When we are judged, it isn't for our justification; Jesus paid that price for us. God rewards us for our works in the Kingdom of God. He pays His laborers.
p: Gift vs wage. We do not earn gifts. A wage is debt owed. In sin, our debt is paid by death and hell, but in Christ we are given grace, a free gift, that we may serve Him, and earn rewards ([[Romans 6:23]]).

# from 3661, 17942, 17527, 12710
--- Gold, silver, or wood, hay and stubble
kicker: The judgment seat
big: 1 Corinthians 3:12-15 | mark: Every man’s work shall be made manifest; he himself shall be saved; yet so as by fire
p: At the Bema seat, wood, hay and stubble does not mean God pulls out a list of your confessed or covered sins to punish you. It means He evaluates the things you did that were worthless for the Kingdom. Time wasted (arguing online), fleshly ambitions, religious works done for show. Burned up: a loss of reward, not an infliction of punishment.
p: Winning souls to Christ, helping the poor and the fatherless, the widows, being doers of the word, those things are rewarded by God in the judgment.

# from 5569, 15000, 10965
--- Ruler over many things
kicker: The judgment seat
big: Matthew 25:21 | mark: thou hast been faithful over a few things, I will make thee ruler over many things
p: In the millennial reign, we who are saved will be appointed to duties, roles and responsibilities, even judge over matters pertaining to God. There shall be thrones, cities and wards, areas of responsibility.
p: These are the crowns we strive for. This is why we humble ourselves and serve those in need. This is where the least among us, meek and lowly, become first in the Kingdom of God ([[Mark 9:35]]).

# from 5651, 5985, 17285
--- Crowns
kicker: The judgment seat
big: 1 Thessalonians 2:19 | mark: what is our hope, or joy, or crown of rejoicing?
p: Every soul we help bring towards Christ, whether a seed sown, watered or harvested, is our glory and joy in Christ's coming. A crown given us, a precious stone, after the wood, hay and stubble are burned away.
p: *A crown of righteousness... unto all them also that love his appearing* ([[2 Timothy 4:8]]). Failure to deliver them that are drawn unto death by claiming ignorance is not an excuse ([[Proverbs 24:11-12]]).
