read: app:doctrine-judgment~10477 | Jesus will judge every man by his works
read: app:doctrine-judgment~5569 | The talents: same joy, different rule

=== The end of the wicked
# from 6235, 5573, 5574, 8163
--- Hell is real
kicker: The end of the wicked
big: Mark 9:43-44 | mark: Where their worm dieth not, and the fire is not quenched
p: This isn't allegory. It's not a parable. It isn't a mistranslation of the Greek, or a later doctrine cobbled together by extra-Biblical sources. *Depart from me, ye cursed, into everlasting fire... And these shall go away into everlasting punishment* ([[Matthew 25:41-46]]).
p: The torment of the damned takes place in the presence of the Lamb ([[Revelation 14:10-11]]). Some use corrupt versions to claim Sheol differs from Hades, or that “Abraham's bosom” is a place rather than a body part. Hell is very real, and God is not slack regarding His promises.

# from 16977, 9565
--- Eternal torment, not annihilation
kicker: The end of the wicked
big: Luke 16:23-24 | mark: I am tormented in this flame
p: Many have turned out to declare the false doctrine of “annihilationism,” that there is no eternal torment in store for the unbeliever. While the widow of a believer can take comfort in their rest, the unbeliever is going to eternal torment, their wealth motheaten and dust ([[Job 27:8]]).
p: We shouldn't draw doctrine from parables taken literally. But Heaven and Hell are real, fixed places, and the destination of the dead, saved or unsaved.

# from 8354
--- The great white throne
kicker: The end of the wicked
big: Revelation 20:12 | mark: the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works
p: The Great White Throne judgment is of the dead. The damned, great and small, whose names were blotted out of the Book of Life. Judged by the books of the law, the scriptures of God, written in our hearts, His wrath written in all of creation, that man may have no excuse.
p: No where in scripture does it say any one gets written into the Book of Life. It was written before creation, and contains every one that lives, who are blotted out if they be reprobate or die without the testimony of Jesus ([[Psalms 69:28]]).

# from 15797, 15348, 15350, 5549, 17746
--- Vengeance is mine
kicker: The end of the wicked
big: Romans 12:19 | mark: Vengeance is mine; I will repay, saith the Lord
p: God's love towards us, mercy and forgiveness, His grace, requires His wrath upon the ungodly. They cannot be separated. Why do bad things happen? Men decide to do them. God visits evil upon evil.
p: *Punished with everlasting destruction from the presence of the Lord* ([[2 Thessalonians 1:9]]). When we despair that the unrighteous prosper, we should praise God that vengeance is His. He will repay.

# from 10719, 15349, 18025
--- Thou that judgest
kicker: The end of the wicked
big: Romans 2:1 | mark: thou that judgest doest the same things
p: If we judge them in their sin against the law, we need to remember we are judged by the same law with the same end, absent Christ. His wrath and our guilt in the law should bring us to repentance, towards the Gospel.
p: The wicked try to silence preaching of the word against them, because the word of God shames them ([[Micah 2:6]]). *God shall likewise destroy thee for ever* ([[Psalms 52:5]]).
read: app:doctrine-judgment~5574 | Everlasting fire, everlasting punishment
read: app:doctrine-judgment~16977 | Eternal torment, not annihilationism
read: app:doctrine-judgment~8354 | The White Throne Judgment of the Dead

=== The hope of the resurrection
# from 16928, 16908
--- I know that my redeemer liveth
kicker: The hope of the resurrection
big: Job 19:25-26 | mark: For I know that my redeemer liveth; yet in my flesh shall I see God
p: Job notes the brevity of life, like a flower cut down. But there is hope of a tree. Even if the stock die in the ground, a little water can bring it to bud again ([[Job 14:7-9]]). Men die, and shall not be raised until the judgment.

# from 4768, 6360, 13685
--- Absent from the body
kicker: The hope of the resurrection
big: 2 Corinthians 5:8 | mark: absent from the body, and to be present with the Lord
p: Our souls go to Heaven, not sleep or instantly regain consciousness at the resurrection as if no time had passed. The souls of the righteous cry out “how long?” ([[Revelation 6:10]]). We still exist within time as the created.
p: In the resurrection, our glorified bodies will be like the angels, who neither marry ([[Mark 12:25]]). And all babies go to Heaven: Job wished he died at birth, to be at rest ([[Job 3:11-13]]).
read: app:doctrine-judgment~16928 | I know that my redeemer liveth
read: app:doctrine-judgment~4768 | Absent from the body, present with the Lord

=== Behold, now
--- Now Is the Day of Salvation [title]
overline: Judgment, hell & the resurrection
heading: Now Is the Day
big: 2 Corinthians 6:2 | mark: behold, now is the day of salvation
center: If you have not believed on Jesus Christ as the ONLY means of forgiveness and righteousness, if you have been called to the wedding feast but have made excuse, repent.
